AB  - The introduction of autonomous vehicles (AVs) in urban mobility represents an opportunity to revolutionize land use, transport efficiency, safety and environmental sustainability. This paper investigates critical strategic leadership approaches optimized to achieve successful AVs deployment on city streets using modern technologies, based on machine learning algorithms fused with perception sensors, V2X communication and agent-based traffic simulation. Using case studies of the top smart cities, this paper identifies best practices and strategic methodologies which have led to effective AV implementation in these areas, particularly in terms of congestion reduction, land use planning and sustainability. Collaboration with public stakeholders and proactive leadership for sustainable transport not only reduce traffic and emissions, but also foster economic development and social equity. Such insights emphasize the capacity of AVs to contribute to more human-centric, endurable metropolises.
